{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Train Models with Levanter (from README)\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook follows the steps from the README to install Levanter and run training commands.\n",
        "\n",
        "It demonstrates:\n",
        "- Installing Levanter in editable mode\n",
        "- Training a GPT-2 \"nano\" model\n",
        "- Training a Llama-small model on OpenWebText with configuration overrides\n",
        "\n",
        "Notes:\n",
        "- If you use Weights & Biases (W&B), run `wandb login` before training.\n",
        "- GPU/TPU setup is platform-specific; see docs for GPU/TPU guides.\n",
        "- This notebook assumes it is located in the `notebooks/` folder of the repo." 
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 0) Set working directory to the repo root\n",
        "So relative config paths like `config/gpt2_nano.yaml` work as in the README."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "# Move from notebooks/ to the repo root\n",
        "os.chdir('..')\n",
        "print('CWD:', os.getcwd())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1) Install Levanter (editable)\n",
        "Per the README, after installing JAX for your platform, install Levanter.\n",
        "If running from this repo, editable install keeps changes live."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "pip"
        ]
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%pip install -e .\n",
        "\n",
        "# Optional: W&B for logging\n",
        "# %pip install wandb\n",
        "# !wandb login  # or set WANDB_API_KEY env var"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2) Verify imports and devices"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import jax\n",
        "import levanter\n",
        "print('JAX devices:', jax.devices())\n",
        "print('Levanter version:', getattr(levanter, '__version__', 'dev'))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3) Train a GPT-2 \"nano\" (from README)\n",
        "This mirrors the README's quickstart. It trains on WikiText-103 by default."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "scrolled": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python -m levanter.main.train_lm --config_path config/gpt2_nano.yaml"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Alternative (without editable install)\n",
        "If you didn't install with `-e .`, you can run the module via its source path:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# !python src/levanter/main/train_lm.py --config_path config/gpt2_nano.yaml"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4) Train a Llama-small on your own data (from README)\n",
        "You can override dataset fields via CLI flags. Here we set `--data.id openwebtext`.\n",
        "Optionally, you may set a tokenizer and/or a cache directory."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "scrolled": true
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!python -m levanter.main.train_lm --config_path config/llama_small_fast.yaml --data.id openwebtext"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Example with tokenizer and cache dir (edit and uncomment to use):\n",
        "# !python -m levanter.main.train_lm \\\n+        "#   --config_path config/llama_small_fast.yaml \\\n+        "#   --data.id openwebtext \\\n+        "#   --data.tokenizer \"NousResearch/Llama-2-7b-hf\" \\\n+        "#   --data.cache_dir \"gs://path/to/cache/dir\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5) Customize a config (reference)\n",
        "Edit YAML under `config/` to change model and training params. For reference, here's the `llama_small_fast.yaml` mentioned in the README."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "print(Path('config/llama_small_fast.yaml').read_text())"
      ]
    }
  ],
